{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 34, "timestamp": 1788792702, "title": "Usenami Signer — reading The Graph, verifying the indexer, deciding", "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/zsh", "TERM": "xterm-256color"}}
[22.565033042,"o","\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n1. The agent asks the price. This is free — reading a 402 costs nothing.\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n"]
[22.717074084,"o","  the gateway asks 0.01 USDC on eip155:8453\n"]
[22.717236834,"o","  payment method: eip3009, token \"USD Coin\" v2\n"]
[44.718875334,"o","\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2. The answer carries the indexer’s signature. We check it over the EXACT bytes.\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n"]
[44.761208667,"o","  responseCID matched: \u001b[33mtrue\u001b[39m\n"]
[44.761335042,"o","  recovered allocation address: 0xfDA28033222bE885965EB5c3011cc2280B7E3e99\n"]
[66.764519,"o","\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n3. Who stands behind that signature. This is an on-chain read — an enclave cannot do it.\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n"]
[66.89373675,"o","  staked indexer: 0x4e5c87772C29381bCaBC58C3f182B6633B5a274a\n"]
[66.893819667,"o","  and the allocation is for THIS subgraph: 0xcd25cb3fc522dabb…\n"]
[88.895832334,"o","\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4. A SECOND STEP, AND IT DOES NOT FOLLOW FROM THE FIRST: are the data usable?\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n"]
[88.896050084,"o","  live read → usable ONDO = 0.3550922693783637012933167398139729\n  same answer, TSLAon → REFUSED: price_absent_or_zero\n  zero is legitimate for a long-tail token and useless as a reference — refuse, not \"free\".\n"]
[88.903944084,"o","  sample 2 → signature verified: true, but the data: REFUSED — graphql_errors\n"]
[88.903968917,"o","  a paid, correctly attested answer WITH AN ERROR AND NO DATA.\n  \"the signature verified\" does not mean \"a price was obtained\".\n"]
[110.907767542,"o","\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n5. A trap you see only if you measure TWO ages.\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n"]
[110.908010084,"o","  subgraph head fresh, price written long ago → price_stale\n  prices are written in event handlers: a dead market = a dead price under green indexing.\n"]
[132.909959209,"o","\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n6. And the decision that follows from it.\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n"]
[132.91179825,"o","  snapshot assembled: 1145 bytes, signed VERBATIM\n"]
[132.911837375,"o","  source age: block 25904639, price from 25904639\n  band ±5%: 0.3373376559… … 0.3728468828…\n"]
[132.9122605,"o","  honest price  → ALLOWED\n"]
[132.912363,"o","  price doubled → REFUSED\n"]
[132.912382875,"o","  the snapshot names what we did NOT check: requestCID, and whether the indexer is right.\n"]
[154.913786667,"o","\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n7. The gate: an agent with no human behind it GETS NO SIGNATURE.\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n"]
[155.3253355,"o","  decision: refused_before_signature\n"]
[155.325416875,"o","  reason: no_registered_human\n  asked: base:absent · worldchain:absent\n  \n  this is a CHANGE OF BEHAVIOUR, not a log line: there will be no signature.\n  \"no human\" is not \"could not ask\": the second has its own reason,\n  because the fix differs — onboard the agent, or repair a broken node.\n  decided by: gateway_before_enclave — before the enclave, not inside it.\n"]
[177.32712675,"o","\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8. The boundary, said out loud.\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n"]
[177.327238834,"o","  everything above runs OUTSIDE the enclave: it has no network.\n  the indexer attestation goes into the snapshot as an artifact anyone can re-check,\n  but OUR signature is what vouches for the snapshot — and we answer for checking the chain.\n  the gate sits BEFORE a signature is requested; this package does not request one yet,\n  so the honest wording is \"no signature is requested\", not \"we guard the signature\".\n\n"]
